{"id":"bounce","title":"When one bounce becomes two","blurb":"A ball dropped on a plate that is shaking up and down settles into a rhythm: one bounce per shake. Turn the shaking up slightly and the rhythm splits \u2014 a high bounce, then a low one, repeating forever. It is the first step of the route to chaos, and it has a sharp threshold.","finding":"The split happens at a shake strength of exactly \u221a(c\u00b2 + (2(1+e\u00b2)/(1+e)\u00b2)\u00b2) = 1.5268 for e = 0.5. At 0.94 of it every impact lands at the same speed 3.1416; at 1.04 they alternate between 3.6157 and 2.6384. Push to 1.1 and it doubles again.","view":[0,-1.8321884406228728,50.2255,4.885835841660995],"kind":"path","tracks":[{"label":"steady: one bounce per cycle","pts":[[0.0,0.9814],[0.0401,1.1064],[0.0801,1.2297],[0.1201,1.3514],[0.1601,1.4715],[0.2001,1.5901],[0.2402,1.707],[0.2802,1.8223],[0.3202,1.936],[0.3602,2.0481],[0.4002,2.1586],[0.4403,2.2675],[0.4803,2.3748],[0.5203,2.4806],[0.5603,2.5847],[0.6003,2.6872],[0.6404,2.7881],[0.6804,2.8874],[0.7204,2.9851],[0.7604,3.0812],[0.8004,3.1757],[0.8405,3.2686],[0.8805,3.3598],[0.9205,3.4495],[0.9605,3.5376],[1.0005,3.6241],[1.0406,3.709],[1.0806,3.7923],[1.1206,3.874],[1.1606,3.954],[1.2006,4.0325],[1.2407,4.1094],[1.2807,4.1847],[1.3207,4.2584],[1.3607,4.3304],[1.4007,4.4009],[1.4408,4.4698],[1.4808,4.537],[1.5208,4.6027],[1.5608,4.6668],[1.6008,4.7292],[1.6409,4.7901],[1.6809,4.8494],[1.7209,4.907],[1.7609,4.9631],[1.8009,5.0175],[1.841,5.0704],[1.881,5.1216],[1.921,5.1713],[1.961,5.2193],[2.001,5.2658],[2.0411,5.3106],[2.0811,5.3539],[2.1211,5.3955],[2.1611,5.4356],[2.2011,5.474],[2.2412,5.5108],[2.2812,5.5461],[2.3212,5.5797],[2.3612,5.6117],[2.4012,5.6422],[2.4413,5.671],[2.4813,5.6982],[2.5213,5.7238],[2.5613,5.7479],[2.6013,5.7703],[2.6414,5.7911],[2.6814,5.8103],[2.7214,5.8279],[2.7614,5.844],[2.8015,5.8584],[2.8415,5.8712],[2.8815,5.8824],[2.9215,5.892],[2.9615,5.9],[3.0016,5.9064],[3.0416,5.9112],[3.0816,5.9144],[3.1216,5.916],[3.1616,5.